On 0.083: it is not too small.  At n = 5 the exact null puts 2 of
120 pairings at |rho| = 1.00 and 8 more at |rho| = 0.90, so the two
smallest two-sided p it can return are 2/120 = 0.017 and
10/120 = 0.083.  The observed rho = +0.90 lands on the second of
them.  It is the closest to significance the sweep could come
without being a perfect ordering, and it still does not reach 0.05.
